# Bundled binaries and runtimes. All of these are staged by the deployment package and are
# re-obtainable from the complete package or a fresh install -- none of them are source.
# Together they are ~1.7 GB; keeping them out is what makes `git log` usable here.
#
# `models/` also covers the manual `models/laya-multilingual.bak` checkpoint kept before a weight
# update. Weights are deliberately untracked: 614 MB of safetensors has no useful diff, and the
# rollback story is a copy of the directory, not a git checkout.
#
# `ra2-api/` was removed: it held @chronodivide/game-api, which nothing in this repo imported.
# Only its node_modules rule lingers, in case a future path reintroduces it.
models/
wheels/
.laya-venv/
node_modules/
ra2-api/node_modules/

# Captured request payloads from `--dump-states`, plus the A/B arms. Regenerated by
# run-baseline.cmd / run-slim.cmd. ~58 MB of throwaway tuning data.
.preview/

# `dist/` stays ignored, as upstream has it: their CI builds from source and publishes the zip, so a
# committed build would only ever be a stale copy of src/. `npm test` builds before running, which is
# what the two dist/-reading tests rely on.
dist/

# Runtime state written by tools/laya-ctl.ps1. The server's stdout/stderr redirection lands in the
# repo root as .laya-server.{out,err}.log, not in logs/ -- the pid file and the LAN token
# (%USERPROFILE%\.laya-server-token, outside the repo) are listed for completeness.
logs/
.laya-server.pid
.laya-server-token
.laya-server.out.log
.laya-server.err.log

# Built extension packages: the zip of the same tree dist/ holds, so it is not worth storing twice.
artifacts/

# Python bytecode. Note tools/__pycache__/laya-serve-local.cpython-313.pyc is already present and
# untracked; the cpython-313 tag pins it to the wheels' Python version.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local Laya decision logs (npm run laya -- --log laya.jsonl). Kept from upstream's ignore list.
*.jsonl
*.ndjson
*.zip

# Editor / OS noise.
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local secrets. The LAN token lives at %USERPROFILE%\.laya-server-token (outside the repo), but a
# manual run may drop one here.
.env
.env.*
*.local